{"case_id":"T8028","gap_exists":true,"gap_type":["configuration","input semantics","API protocol","state","attack surface"],"commit_induced":"YES","maintenance_needed":true,"confidence":99,"affected_functions":["simdjson::dom::parser::number_as_string(bool)","simdjson::dom::parser::parse_into_document","tape_builder::visit_number","simdjson::dom::element::get_bigint","simdjson::dom::element::is_bigint","print_json"],"reason":"S1 adds an opt-in parser mode, `parser::number_as_string(bool)`, that changes oversized-integer inputs from `BIGINT_ERROR` into successful `BIGINT` elements. H0 constructs `simdjson::dom::parser parser` but never enables `_number_as_string`, whose declared default is `false`, so fuzz input cannot reach the new successful-big-integer path in `tape_builder::visit_number` or exercise the new `get_bigint`/`is_bigint` API behavior. Moreover, `print_json` has no `element_type::BIGINT` case, so merely enabling the mode would still leave the new element variant unconsumed. This gap did not exist in S0 because neither the configuration nor the `BIGINT` element path existed there.","evidence":["`parser.h` adds `number_as_string(bool enabled)` and initializes `_number_as_string{false}`.","`parser::parse_into_document` copies `_number_as_string` into `implementation->_number_as_string`.","`tape_builder::visit_number` converts `BIGINT_ERROR` to `SUCCESS` and appends `internal::tape_type::BIGINT` only when `iter.dom_parser._number_as_string` is true.","H0 calls `parser.parse(Data, Size)` on a default-constructed parser and contains no call to `parser.number_as_string(true)`.","S1 adds `element_type::BIGINT`, `element::get_bigint`, and `element::is_bigint`, while H0's `print_json` switch handles only ARRAY, OBJECT, INT64, UINT64, DOUBLE, STRING, BOOL, and NULL_VALUE."],"recommended_action":"Extend H0 to fuzz both `number_as_string(false)` and `number_as_string(true)` states, and add an `element_type::BIGINT` branch that calls `get_bigint()` and consumes the returned raw digit string; optionally exercise `is_bigint()` and serialization for the same parsed element."}
